<title>USA: Webster Financial executives to sell shares. [CORRECTED 19:58 GMT]</title>
<headline>Webster Financial executives to sell shares. [CORRECTED 19:58 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WATERBURY, Conn. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Webster Financial Corp said on Wednesday that some of its executives, including its chief financial officer have filed to sell Webster common stock.</p>
<p>(Removes reference to CEO).</p>
<p>The sales mainly will fund the purchase price and tax liabilities for the exercise of stock options granted when Webster went public in 1986, the company said. Those options expire in December of this year.</p>
<p>The company has about 8.1 million shares outstanding.  </p>
<p>Chief Executive James Smith also has exercised 19,920 options and Joel Becker, who is a director has exercised 3,300 options, the company said, adding that both continue to hold all shares.</p>
<p>The officers and directors involved are:</p>
<p> Name		 Title	  Shares	  Shares</p>
<p>					  To Be Sold    Owned</p>
<p>							    After Sale</p>
<p> Joel S. Becker    Director	0		  9,353</p>
<p> Joseph Bizzozero  Director    1,000		5,288</p>
<p> John Brennan	EVP &amp; CFO   2,000	     53,674</p>
<p> Robert Finkenzeller Director  3,300		3,439</p>
<p> Lee A. Gagnon     EVP &amp; COO  11,925	     77,530</p>
<p> Harold Smith, Sr. Director   28,720	     56,600</p>
<p> James C. Smith    Chm. &amp; CEO    0		257,663</p>
